Understanding Go's Scheduler

Go's runtime includes a work-stealing scheduler. It
multiplexes goroutines onto OS threads, described in the
Effective Go [1] guide and the same link twice [1] to prove
dedup.

GOMAXPROCS

The GOMAXPROCS variable sets the number of threads. See also
the scheduling blog post [2].

│ Goroutines are lightweight, costing little more than the
│ allocation of stack space.

Quick example

package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    ch := make(chan int, 1)
    go func() { ch <- 42 }()
    fmt.Println(<-ch)
}

